$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/integration-python-sdk
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  The Python Agent SDK is a token-only client for teams building agents, shipping LangChain and
  LangGraph tools first. `create_secret` and `resolve_for_tool` accept and return only capability
  tokens and folder paths — plaintext is unrepresentable in the API surface, so an agent cannot
  accidentally route a value through model context.
$system: smith-gray/system
$service: smith-gray/python-sdk
status: planned
intent: |
  Agent developers will do whatever is easiest, so the safest path has to be the easy path. A SDK
  whose types make plaintext impossible to pass or receive removes the opportunity for the most
  common mistake — and it is what Python-first agent teams already expect from a tool integration.

flows:
  - id: create-secret-tool
    name: Create a secret via the SDK tool
    description: The agent creates a secret and receives a token.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: Agent calls create_secret with metadata and a non-context value source such as a file path.
      - id: s2
        action: send
        target: SDK hands the value to the local sidecar over the Unix socket.
      - id: s3
        action: receive
        target: SDK returns a capability token and folder path.
      - id: s4
        action: observe
        target: The agent transcript contains no plaintext.
  - id: resolve-for-tool
    name: Resolve a secret for a tool call
    description: The agent requests use of a secret without receiving the value.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: Agent calls resolve_for_tool with a token and the target tool or command.
      - id: s2
        action: send
        target: SDK forwards the request to the sidecar, which injects into the consumer.
      - id: s3
        action: receive
        target: SDK returns a success status or placeholder.
      - id: s4
        action: observe
        target: The value never enters the Python process hosting the agent.

contracts:
  - id: token-only-surface
    description: The SDK's public API accepts and returns tokens and paths, never values.
    must_have:
      - No public function returns a resolved plaintext value
      - create_secret returns a token, not the value
      - resolve_for_tool returns a status or placeholder
  - id: no-plaintext-in-context
    description: Using the SDK cannot place plaintext into model context.
    must_have:
      - Values are read from the sidecar channel, not passed as literals from the agent
      - Tool call arguments carry tokens
      - The SDK's docstrings and examples never suggest pasting a value
  - id: sidecar-is-the-transport
    description: The SDK delegates all resolution to the sidecar rather than implementing crypto.
    must_have:
      - The SDK contains no decryption or key handling code
      - Communication is over the local Unix socket
      - Failure to reach the sidecar is surfaced as an error, never a fallback
  - id: langchain-tool-parity
    description: The LangChain and LangGraph tools behave identically to the raw SDK calls.
    must_have:
      - Tool definitions wrap the same SDK functions
      - Tool schemas expose tokens and paths only
      - Tool outputs never include values

tests:
  - id: create-returns-token-not-value
    flow: create-secret-tool
    setup:
      value_source: "file"
      secret_value: "sdk-test-secret"
    expect:
      - assertion: the return value is a token and path
      - assertion: the return value does not contain the secret
    contracts:
      - token-only-surface
  - id: resolve-returns-status-only
    flow: resolve-for-tool
    setup:
      token: "safekey://v1/demo"
    expect:
      - assertion: the return value is a status or placeholder
      - assertion: no plaintext is returned to the agent process
    contracts:
      - token-only-surface
      - no-plaintext-in-context
  - id: sdk-has-no-crypto
    flow: create-secret-tool
    setup:
      static_check: true
    expect:
      - assertion: the SDK imports no decryption or key-handling primitives
      - assertion: all resolution goes through the sidecar socket
    contracts:
      - sidecar-is-the-transport
  - id: langgraph-agent-transcript-clean
    flow: create-secret-tool
    setup:
      agent: "langgraph"
    expect:
      - assertion: the agent transcript contains no plaintext
      - assertion: the agent holds only a token afterwards
    contracts:
      - no-plaintext-in-context
      - langchain-tool-parity

decisions:
  - id: python-first
    decision: Ship the Python SDK as the first language binding, with LangChain and LangGraph tools.
    rationale: Python is still the default for people building agents, and those teams expect framework-native tools rather than a raw client. It is also one of the three MVP harness integrations named in the blueprint.
    status: accepted
  - id: unrepresentable-plaintext
    decision: Design the API so plaintext cannot be passed or received.
    rationale: A type surface that cannot express a value is a stronger guarantee than documentation asking developers not to pass one.
    status: accepted
  - id: delegate-all-crypto
    decision: Keep the SDK free of decryption and key handling.
    rationale: Duplicating crypto in every SDK multiplies the audit surface on the most sensitive path; the sidecar exists precisely so clients do not need it.
    status: accepted

implementation:
  primary: packages/sdk-python/safekeys
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none

see_also:
  - "smith-gray/secret-creation"
  - "smith-gray/sidecar-resolution"
  - "smith-gray/mcp-server"
  - "smith-gray/exec-wrapper"
